tools/fmm3d/hfmm3d-levels.patch: per-level timers and a plane-wave level switch in FMM3D
v2.1.0's hfmm3dmain (src/Helmholtz/hfmm3d.f), Helmholtz CH6.2d (docs/helmholtz/tasks/CH6.2d.md).
tools/fmm3d/build.sh applies it (patch -p1 in the unpacked FMM3D-2.1.0) to the variants
`timed` and `fastker-timed`; README.md beside it documents the switch and the lines.

- Per level, wall times (omp_get_wtime) of step 3: on a plane-wave level the setup
  (hwts3e to the zeroed waves), list 4's waves (h3dlist4pw), the multipoles to waves and the
  parents' loop, with the thread-seconds of its plane-wave part and of list 3 inside it; on a
  point-and-shoot level its M2L loop and its list-3 loops; list 4 on point-and-shoot levels.
  Printed after each call, one `hfmm3d-level:` line per level and one `hfmm3d-steps:` line.
- FMM3D_PW_LEVEL (environment): unset, FMM3D's own choice of the regime per level; an
  integer l >= 2, only level l may take plane waves (where FMM3D's tests allow them) and
  every other plane-wave level takes FMM3D's point-and-shoot path; -1, none does.
No value is computed differently: the timers read the clock and the switch only chooses
between FMM3D's own two code paths.

